// Mobs. Adding one is an entry here plus, if it behaves differently, an AI
// in src/entity/ai.rs. Values are modern Minecraft's on normal difficulty.
//
// Fields:
//   name, texture (a resource location: entity/pig/temperate_pig), health
//   width, height    hitbox in blocks
//   speed            walking speed as a fraction of the player's
//   ai               Passive, Hostile(attack:), Neutral(attack:), Spider(attack:),
//                    Archer(interval:), Creeper(power:), Enderman(attack:), Slime,
//                    Witch, Phantom(attack:), Swimmer, Wolf(attack:), Cat, Horse,
//                    Rabbit, Bee(attack:), Fox(attack:), Villager, Ghast,
//                    ZombifiedPiglin(attack:), Piglin(attack:), Hoglin(attack:), Strider,
//                    Blaze
//   burns_in_daylight, climbs, swims, flies, hurt_by_water, no_fall,
//   fire_immune (no harm from fire or lava), walks_on_lava (striders)
//   scale            the model is drawn this much bigger
//   eye              eye height as a fraction of the height (default 0.85)
//   variants         other textures a mob may wear (picked by its variant)
//   layers           more models drawn over it, each with a texture: dyed (takes
//                    the mob's color), wool (hidden once sheared), glow (full
//                    bright), only_variant, saddle (shown once saddled)
//   drops            (item, min, max, cooked: item dropped instead while burning,
//                    chance: 0-1)
//   spawn            Never; Ground(blocks, min_light, chance, group, biomes) at world
//                    generation; Dark(max_light, group, biomes, weight, nether)
//                    near the player in the dark (biomes: the Overworld's, all
//                    if empty; nether: [(biome, weight, group)]); Nether(max_light,
//                    biomes: [(biome, weight, group)]); Lava(group, biomes);
//                    Fortress(weight, group) only inside Nether fortresses;
//                    Water(chance, group, biomes, min_depth); SlimeChunk(below);
//                    Phantom
//   model            texture_size and parts in Minecraft model coordinates (pixels,
//                    y down, feet at 24): uv offset, box from and size, pivot,
//                    rest rotation (rest, rest_y, rest_z in radians), grow, and
//                    animation role: None, Head, LegA/LegB (swing opposite),
//                    ArmA/ArmB, Reaching (zombie arms), Aim (skeleton arms),
//                    WingA/WingB, SpiderLeg(n), Tentacle(n), Tail; mirror for
//                    left limbs; extra boxes that move with the part.
